--   The linear fibre: for the linear form α a₀ + β b₀, the fibre always contains the diagonal pair (a₀, b₀), and any other pair for at most q of the q² values of (α, β);…
-- statement:
--   A statement of the module `MIPRE.Background.QLD.Separate` of the MIP\* = RE formalization (commit `70cbf1c` of vidick/MIPRE-formalization). Separating the two point variables (`lem:qld-global-separate`). An outcome `g = α g₁ + β g₂` of the global measurement that is linear in the combining coordinates (`IsLinAB`, `lem:qld-global-linear`) is *good* when `g₁` reads only the `x` block and `g₂` only the `z` block: `g = α g_X(x) + β g_Z(z)` (`IsGood`). This file bounds the weight of the linear outcomes that are not good, from the two ordered-product estimates of `lem:qld-global-products`: the order `X_a Z_b` controls the outcomes whose `g₂` reads a coordinate outside the `z` block, and the order `Z_b X_a` those whose `g₁` reads a…
--
--   **The linear fibre**: for the linear form `α a₀ + β b₀`, the fibre always contains the diagonal
--   pair `(a₀, b₀)`, and any other pair for at most `q` of the `q²` values of `(α, β)`; so the average
--   over `(α, β)` of the fibre weights is at most `2/q · ⟨S ⊗ 1⟩` plus the diagonal weight.
--
--   **Formal statement.** In Lean, with the scope shown:
--
--   ```lean
--   open MIPRE
--   open MIPRE.QLD
--   open Finset Matrix MIPRE MIPRE.LIDT
--   open scoped Kronecker ComplexOrder MatrixOrder
--   variable {F : Type*} [Field F] [Fintype F] [DecidableEq F] {RA RB : Type*} [Fintype RA]
--
--   theorem MIPRE.QLD.sum_ab_snorm_sq_ordComb_le_of_lin (Φ : RA × RB → ℂ) {S : Matrix RA RA ℂ} (hsa : Sᴴ = S)
--       (hidem : S * S = S) (hX : IsPVM X') (hZ : IsPVM Z') (a₀ b₀ : F) :
--       ∑ ab : F × F, ((Fintype.card F : ℝ)⁻¹ * (Fintype.card F : ℝ)⁻¹)
--           * snorm Φ ((aOp S : Matrix (RA × RB) _ ℂ)
--             * bOp (ptComb (ordXZ X' Z') ab.1 ab.2 (ab.1 * a₀ + ab.2 * b₀))) ^ 2
--         ≤ 2 / Fintype.card F * bornProb Φ S 1
--           + snorm Φ ((aOp S : Matrix (RA × RB) _ ℂ) * bOp (X' a₀ * Z' b₀)) ^ 2
--   ```
